# TNFR ${version} development bundle

This lightweight source snapshot preserves the files of commit `${commit}`.
It includes the engine, theory, ontology, contracts, documentation, examples,
tests, instruments and configuration. Research evidence under `docs/assets/`
is available on demand; the small `docs/assets/mathjax.js` site helper remains
included. This is a development starting point, not an offline Python
environment or a complete evidence archive.

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) before making changes. Its contributor rules and
byte-identical agent mirror remain authoritative for this snapshot.

## Start from the maintained owners

- [README](README.md): present model and organized-object example.
- [Theory catalog](theory/README.md): entry to the research sourcebook,
  definitions, conditional proofs, active question and stopping conditions.
- [Architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md), [API contracts](docs/API_CONTRACTS.md),
  [contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md) and [testing](TESTING.md): implementation and
  verification boundaries.

Use local owners for this version. Original documents may link to GitHub
`main`, which can change. The
[version-pinned source](https://github.com/${repository}/tree/${commit})
preserves the selected commit. Packaging does not modify or validate scientific
claims or select a research task.

## Install and run

Extract the ZIP into a normal local directory. From its root, create a separate
Python 3.10+ environment:

```sh
python -m venv .venv
```

Activate with `.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1` in PowerShell or
`source .venv/bin/activate` in a POSIX shell. Then:

```sh
python -m pip install -e .
python -m tnfr --version
python examples/01_foundations/01_hello_world.py
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py verify
```

Dependencies require network access or an appropriate local package cache.
For affected implementation tests, follow `TESTING.md`. Missing evidence is
not a passing result. Some tests, the internal-reference check and the complete
documentation build require the omitted files.

## Recover evidence without rerunning experiments

[bundle/manifest.json](bundle/manifest.json) records included and omitted Git
files, byte sizes, SHA256 hashes and Git blob identifiers. Each omitted file has
a commit-pinned source URL. The recovery helper needs only Python's standard
library:

```sh
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py list
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py fetch --path docs/assets/organized_source_silence_handoff
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py verify
```

Use an exact file path or a directory prefix from the manifest. Downloads
must match the recorded size and SHA256 before installation; differing local
files are never replaced. Recovery does not execute producers, extract nested
ZIPs or select new calculations.

To recover all omitted evidence, explicitly choose:

```sh
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py fetch --all
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py verify --require-all-evidence
```

An existing full GitHub or Zenodo release ZIP can supply the same files offline:

```sh
python scripts/development_bundle_evidence.py fetch --all --archive /path/to/full-release.zip
```

Full restoration adds ${omitted_bytes} bytes of files. Individual downloads may
transfer more than the full compressed archive. The helper uses a filesystem
supporting hard links for atomic installation without overwriting. If that
facility is unavailable, use the full archive in a fresh directory.

Verification reports development edits as byte mismatches. Additional local
files are outside its inventory. Hashes detect differences; they do not
authenticate an untrusted manifest or establish scientific validity.

## Git history and optional supplements

There is no `.git` directory. Initializing a new repository does not recover
the original history. Historical recovery, original pinned worktrees and normal
contribution workflows need a proper clone:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/${repository}.git
cd TNFR-Python-Engine
git switch --detach ${commit}
```

Small inactive applications and recovery records retain their original status.
No tracked file is rewritten for this bundle. Only `START_HERE.md` and
`bundle/manifest.json` are generated packaging aids outside the selected tree.

Separate release supplements are not part of the Git tree or this manifest.
Check the [release assets](https://github.com/${repository}/releases/tag/v${version})
for their own restoration instructions and the complete source archive.
The external `.zip.sha256` file checks this whole lightweight ZIP.
